  "checked": "2018 final: Mbappé, 19, scored France's fourth (65', Lucas Hernández's pass, 25 yards, right foot) in a 4-2 win over Croatia; first teenager since Pelé to score in a final (ESPN, Quartz). 2021 Nations League final: France 2-1 Spain, Mbappé the winner (Wikipedia, UEFA). 2022 final: 3-3, Mbappé hat-trick, Argentina won on pens (Wikipedia, widely reported). 2026: Golden Boot with 10, first two-time winner, now the World Cup's all-time top scorer; France lost the semi 2-0 to Spain (ESPN, Gulf News, WION). Portugal since Mbappé's debut (March 2017): Nations League 2019 and 2025; Euro 2024 QF 0-0, France won 5-3 on pens in Hamburg; Portugal have never reached a World Cup final (Wikipedia, UEFA). The Portugal-Mbappé goal is clearly imagined. Kits in the game footage are plain.",
